# Force LF regardless of the cloning machine's core.autocrlf — a patch/diff file (or a bash
# script meant to run on the organizers' Linux re-run machine) must never pick up CRLF just
# because it happened to be checked out on Windows. Discovered via a real fresh-clone Docker
# reproduction test: a plain Windows `git clone` of this repo (default core.autocrlf=true)
# silently converted every patches/*.diff to CRLF on checkout, which then broke `git apply`
# inside the Linux container it was copied into.
*.diff text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
